      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we use `getrandom()` directly for discriminator allocation? This runs during control-plane session creation, and VPP already uses it when creating IPsec SAs. That would avoid the custom PID/timestamp/address entropy mixing and the extra `bfd_get_session()` argument. We should reject zero, retain the local collision retry, and handle entropy acquisition failures. Cross-instance uniqueness would remain probabilistic with a 32-bit discriminator, so the comments should avoid claiming a guarantee.",
